    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9e2f8f56-df0f-52ab-b741-d610217eab1d",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+36y-20z &=-56 \\\\ x+9y-5z &=-14 \\\\ 4x+36y-20z &=-56\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 36 & -20 & -56 \\\\ 1 & 9 & -5 & -14 \\\\ 4 & 36 & -20 & -56\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1\\leftrightarrow R_2\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 9 & -5 & -14 \\\\ 4 & 36 & -20 & -56 \\\\ 4 & 36 & -20 & -56\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(-4)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 9 & -5 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 36 & -20 & -56\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(-4)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 9 & -5 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n",
